{"base_rate":0.12384716732542819,"brier":0.06162529644268775,"bss":0.43207227003679405,"bss_hi":0.5278057829523417,"bss_lo":0.31697007889361145,"chart":{"base":[222.6,53.3],"fp":[192.9,321.1],"lead":"62,239.8 272,204.8 482,169.1 692,116.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 81% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +11pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 36% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 48% → rained 52%"},"rel":"62,466 72.4,460.1 115.6,434.9 364.9,243.1"},"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.011936758893280636,"ess":401.75132923333433,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nuevo Laredo</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nuevo Laredo rain forecast is genuinely useful, and its stated probabilities are honest throughout.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (72%), believe about\n<b>71%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 759 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLAREDO INTL AP, 8.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 40 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(14&ndash;94) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>303</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>146</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">0 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nuevo Laredo</b> <span class=\"muted\">Mexico</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">probabilities honest throughout</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>14&ndash;94\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>759 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nuevo Laredo &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nuevo Laredo\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 63.84342465753424,367.041095890411 76.83083333333333,341.55555555555554 98.1637037037037,314.5925925925926 146.9425,254.60000000000002 312.6501298701299,88.90909090909088 312.6501298701299,150.36363636363637 146.9425,322.85 98.1637037037037,364.0246913580247 76.83083333333333,376.94444444444446 63.84342465753424,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"336.9196310935441\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"336.9196310935441\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,382.0 63.84342465753424,377.013698630137 76.83083333333333,361.77777777777777 98.1637037037037,350.5432098765432 146.9425,263.7 312.6501298701299,122.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 303 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 2%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 146 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"63.84342465753424\" cy=\"377.013698630137\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"76.83083333333333\" cy=\"361.77777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"98.1637037037037\" cy=\"350.5432098765432\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"146.9425\" cy=\"263.7\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 72%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"312.6501298701299\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(12%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nuevo Laredo the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.46) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.32).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'>0.319</td><td class='num'>3.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.435</td><td class='num'>2.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'>0.457</td><td class='num'>1.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.458</td><td class='num'>4.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":27.47629,"lon":-99.51639,"n":759,"n_cities":213,"name":"Nuevo Laredo","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":303,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.016506849315068493,"n":146,"obs":0.0136986301369863,"sig":false},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.05319444444444445,"n":72,"obs":0.05555555555555555,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.11345679012345679,"n":81,"obs":0.08641975308641975,"sig":false},{"hi":0.39,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.25125000000000003,"n":80,"obs":0.325,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.39,"mean":0.